WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.890
Hi it's Michelle from lab muffin beauty
science here I've had a lot of questions

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:08.490
about my skincare and makeup routine so
today I'm going to be showing you my

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:12.870
morning routine. My evening routine is
much more complicated and much more

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:16.590
variable so I thought I'd start with the
morning routine which is a bit simpler

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:21.270
and then maybe show you guys my evening
routine a bit later. I'm not a makeup

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:24.930
artist I have no idea what I'm doing
with my makeup so I'm probably doing

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:29.670
like 20 things wrong but this seems to
work for me and it's good enough so I'm

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:34.590
sticking to it.
My skin is really dehydration prone so

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:38.399
in the morning I rinsed my face with
water without using cleanser, and pat it

00:00:38.399 --> 00:00:43.530
dry with a towel. I try not to use too
much under my sunscreen so I usually

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:47.160
just use some sort of hydrating spray or
toner. I've been using La Roche

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:50.640
Posay Serozinc for summer but I think
I'll have to switch to something more

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.960
humectant when dry winter weather comes
around. A lot of people have asked me how

00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:00.270
I apply my sunscreen so here it is. My
favorite sunscreen of all time is Ultraceuticals

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:05.100
Ultra UV Protective
Moisturizer. It's light it's not white it

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:09.540
sinks in easily so you can apply lots of
it without any issues. It doesn't clog my

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:14.820
pores and it has Tinosorb S which is
my favorite UVA protective ingredient.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:19.860
It also isn't silicone heavy which is
pretty rare with sunscreens designed for

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:24.600
daily use. I personally find that
silicones make my skin really oily after

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:29.189
a few hours. It also doesn't sting my
eyes so I can put it all over my face

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:33.450
without any issues.
I know it's really expensive but it is

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:37.590
really good. I'm working on some reviews
of some more affordable sunscreen

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:43.290
options so keep an eye out for those. I
use around 3/4 of 1/4 tsp as I worked

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:48.000
out when I put tape all over my face and
I try not to rub it in too much. I have a

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.210
few other videos on how to wear
sunscreen so it's as effective as

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:56.369
possible and I've linked them below in
the caption. Then I wait around 15

00:01:56.369 --> 00:02:00.689
minutes or so before I apply foundation
so that my sunscreen has time to set and

00:02:00.689 --> 00:02:04.710
it won't shift as much. Usually at this
point I'd go off and do my hair and put

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:08.280
on my clothes but for this video I
decided not to be naked

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:14.790
and my hair's already done. Next I apply
foundation. I have a few foundations that

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:18.900
I use a lot but I'm often just testing
out different products so it isn't

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:24.480
really set. I'm blending together l'oreal
infallible pro glow in creamy natural

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:28.290
designer brands luminous hydrating
foundation in porcelain ivory and

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:33.300
nourish london illuminating face shimmer
I used to use matte foundations because

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:37.560
my skin is oily but I found that during
the day I'd get oily in patches and it

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:42.330
looked really obvious. Mixing an
illuminator into my foundation pretty

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:46.860
much fixed that. My skin does get oily
but the contrast between the dry and

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:52.140
oily patches isn't quite so blindingly
obvious. I found out that I can't

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:56.550
actually use this L'Oreal foundation two
days in a row without breaking out which

00:02:56.550 --> 00:03:00.690
is a real pity because it has such a
gorgeous finish so if it works for you

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:05.100
I'm super jealous. I'm patting the
mixture on with a damp ecotools

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:08.780
sponge and trying not to rub so the
sunscreen doesn't move around too much.

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:14.160
I'm really not a morning person so the
sponge is really handy since it doesn't

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:17.760
require too much brainpower and I can
sort of just slap myself in the face

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:24.030
with it. I'm currently using it cosmetics
bye bye under-eye illumination concealer

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:28.530
in medium
I usually don't use too much concealer

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:32.810
under my eyes because it always creases
on me and makes me look even tireder

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:39.000
- tireder - more tired then if I just let
my dark circles hang loose but I use it

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:45.209
everywhere else on my face as well I
like using my finger for concealer

00:03:45.209 --> 00:03:49.470
because I find it easier to control than
a brush plus it means I have less

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:52.190
brushes to wash

00:03:55.420 --> 00:04:01.519
next up is powder I use a starch based
powder after a lot of trial and error I

00:04:01.519 --> 00:04:05.599
found that the best powders for my oily
skin have starch their first ingredient

00:04:05.599 --> 00:04:10.209
I'm using Jurlique's rose silk finishing
powder with a fluffy brush from Ecotools

00:04:10.209 --> 00:04:14.660
sometimes I actually mix regular grocery
cornstarch into it if it's going to be a

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:18.829
hot day and I need more oil control I've
seen a few things online about how you

00:04:18.829 --> 00:04:22.580
can't use cornflour because it's not
specially treated or whatever but you

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:25.580
can use it safely
I have a blog post on it that I've

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:30.889
linked so you can read all about it
the next step is blush and highlighter

00:04:30.889 --> 00:04:36.500
I love the Jaclyn Hill Becca
champagne collection palette I use the

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:43.220
mix of Amaretto and Pamplemousse French
grapefruit blushes sorry mon French is

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:53.510
le crap and then I put some champagne
pop on top I'm using a real techniques

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:59.870
brush to apply the blush and the
highlighter I used the regular part for

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:04.550
blush and the side for illuminator which
I'm sure is blasphemy but I've been

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:07.789
reassured by two qualified makeup
artists that there are no rules in

00:05:07.789 --> 00:05:13.639
makeup so I do what I want at this
point I usually realize I've put on too

00:05:13.639 --> 00:05:17.389
much blush and blend it out with the
Ecotools brush again I'm not that

00:05:17.389 --> 00:05:19.990
skilled at makeup

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:29.470
I'm using Loreal brow artist expert
mechanical brow pencil in Ebony for my

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:34.660
brows for the longest time it was
impossible to find a brow product that

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:38.500
wasn't too red for me but this new
range has greys and browns which is

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:43.380
awesome because it means I don't have to
buy Korean brow products online anymore

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:47.920
my brows are microbladed but there are a
few spots where the pigment didn't

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:53.440
implant well so it's a little bit patchy
mostly I just leave them because I was

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:57.730
never that good at doing my brows anyway
so my slightly patchy microbladed brows

00:05:57.730 --> 00:06:02.110
are a million times better than my old
brows but I'm putting in effort because

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:10.570
I'm filming I have a really simple eye
shadow process I've seen tutorials where

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:14.140
they really gradually put on eye shadow
and it looks amazingly blended and

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:20.110
gorgeous but I'm too impatient for that
I really like sleep so I like my whole

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:24.370
beauty routine to be like 15 minutes
long and most days I don't even use

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:30.370
eyeshadow so this is my quick and dirty
routine I start with etude house proof

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:36.940
10 eye primer so my eyeshadow sticks on
evenly I usually go for shimmery

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:42.610
eyeshadow because it's a bit more
forgiving and easier to blend I'm using

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:47.080
the shade Venus from the Garbo and Kelly
overnight sensation palette with a real

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:53.100
techniques eyeshadow brush and putting
it all over my lid as the base color

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:03.460
then I use a pencil brush from bdellium
to add a darker shade Pandora and pat it

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:13.090
on the outside corner then I use the
Real Techniques brush again and blend

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:21.460
the two shades together I use a clean
ish fluffy Bdellium brush to blend the

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:32.979
edge of the eyeshadow and hope that it
looks okay I actually got semi-permanent

00:07:32.979 --> 00:07:37.630
eyeliner done recently after using
pencil eyeliner for about 15 years I'm

00:07:37.630 --> 00:07:41.770
putting a little extra on here for
filming purposes and because the eye

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:45.729
shadow is covered up a bit but mostly
I've been just going out the door

00:07:45.729 --> 00:07:50.590
without doing anything. actually I
normally did this anyway because I do my

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:55.539
eyeliner and lipstick on the train I
like my sleep I don't bump anyone I

00:07:55.539 --> 00:08:00.159
don't spread my stuff everywhere
no one gets eyeliner on them I'm quieter

00:08:00.159 --> 00:08:05.409
than people talking on the phone just
let me live my life my eyeliner is from

00:08:05.409 --> 00:08:09.970
girlee cosmetics which is a makeup artist
type brand that has stalls at expos

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:14.949
but doesn't really sell direct I
discovered them by chance and it's been

00:08:14.949 --> 00:08:19.870
the first pencil eyeliner that didn't
transfer on my oily lids so I've stuck

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:25.690
by it I'm too scared to change I don't
usually wear mascara a few people have

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:29.530
asked me about this it's because I have
that hair-pulling disorder that I'm

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:33.789
probably going to say wrong
trichotillomania and it usually happens

00:08:33.789 --> 00:08:38.919
when I'm stressed which is quite a lot
so my eyelashes are usually too uneven

00:08:38.919 --> 00:08:45.250
for mascara to look good once that's
done I miss my face with a setting spray

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:51.730
I'm currently using Algenist splash
which has a really nice fine mist it

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:55.300
makes everything look less powdery and
more like actual human skin and

00:08:55.300 --> 00:09:00.490
hopefully keeps it intact a bit more
during the day but I'm super oily so

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:03.450
usually that doesn't happen

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:13.400
today I'm using synergie lipglo in
tea rose I really like this lip gloss it's

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:17.840
more pigmented than the usual lip gloss
but it doesn't clump up it's very sticky

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:31.580
so it stays in place and it's really
moisturizing so that's my morning

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:35.840
routine I hope you found this video
interesting if you liked it and if you

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:40.340
want to find out more about science - more
sciency stuff in this video anyway - you

00:09:40.340 --> 00:09:43.910
can look at my channel which has lots of
videos I've also got my blog which has

00:09:43.910 --> 00:09:47.210
lots and lots of posts about beauty
science you can also follow me on

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:51.680
Instagram where I put lots and lots of
science-based beauty tips see you next

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:59.160
time :)

